<p>This is cool enough conceptually for an upvote, though I'm left wondering about a few things.</p>
<p>How exactly are these creatures being observed? <em>They</em> might be able to move through stone as if it was water, but light certainly can't. We'd only be able to directly observe objects that are touching the surface(s) of the stone, unless some sort of sonic imaging is in use.</p>
<p>Also, I'd ditch the suggestion that these are "organisms that adapted to life in solid rock", it sounds a bit silly.</p>

