			<div class="content" id="post-content-759681">
									

<p>This is one of those SCPs that handily makes up for a lack of creepy by generating a sense of wonder. Upvoted.</p>
<p>Now, down to brass tacks. Given how hard these lifeforms are to recapture or destroy if they escape containment, would this qualify for a Euclid rating? Also, it might be interesting to see the Founation intentionally allow some of them into a sample of concrete, then perform tests on the fossils and/or the concrete. How does having these things inside it affect the strength of a stone or concrete? If their presence weakens it, then these things pose a credible threat to a lot of structures if they ever become widespread. How finely-pulverized are disposed-of materials? A grain of sand is significantly larger than a microbe, which means there could be fossilized plankton swimming around all over the place.</p>

							</div>

								
					
